==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Zoge]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 10~20 seconds<sup>300f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Znache]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 10~20 seconds<sup>300f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*2 [[Cadaver Bear]]s spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>.
*2 [[Teacher Bear]]s spawn, delay 66.67 seconds<sup>2,000f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 5 seconds<sup>150f</sup>, delay 16.67~26.67 seconds<sup>500f~800f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**Infinite [[B.B.Bunny|B.B.Bunnies]] spawn, delay 6~12 seconds<sup>180f~360f</sup>.
**1 [[Teacher Bear]] spawns.

==Strategy==
This stage is at its hardest when both Cadaver Bears are alive at once, especially on higher difficulties. Try to vanquish the first Cadaver Bear with a ranged [[:Category:Zombie Killer Cats|Zombie Killer]] such as [[Talents|Talented]] [[Archer Cat (Rare Cat)|Cataur]] or [[Ototo Corps|Holy Blast]] to make this a fair fight.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong Cat]] - Shigong can tank multiple hits from Cadaver Bear thanks to being [[Resistant]] against Zombies.
*[[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Slime Cat]] - Slime Cat's [[Wave Attack]], when timed perfectly, can knock back the Teacher Bear easily and kill peons.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Sharpshooter Saki (Uber Rare Cat)|Nighthunter Saki]] - Nighthunter Saki's range allows her to safely attack Cadaver Bear, and along with her [[Zombie Killer]], she can easily turn this stage into a joke.
*[[Mighty Kristul Muu (Legend Rare Cat)|Doom Engine Pandora]] - Pandora can kill the Cadaver Bears easily, and their quick attack rate is also useful for knocking back the Teacher Bears and Doge Darks.
*[[Hyper Battalion Convoys]] - While only in true form, their knockback can help keep those bears at bay. Even if a non-Zombie Killer gets one, they will take care of the body with their [[Soulstrike]].

